# ICN Jobs Literature Review — Index

Master catalog of all wiki pages and their relationships. Populated automatically after ingest.

## Studies

Key research studies and reports:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[ferdman-2026-ai-deskilling-structural-problem]] | 2026-07-10 | 2026-09-25 | Avigail Ferdman's 2026 paper in AI & Society presenting a structural analysis of how AI systems can undermine human capacities through systemic environmental conditions rather than individual failings. Introduces the critical distinction between capacity-hostile and capacity-conducive environments, analyzes the role of agential control and habituation in capacity development, and examines how Artificial Personal Assistants may create capacity-hostile environments by encouraging plan-following rather than plan-forming. The paper argues that deskilling should be understood as a structural problem requiring societal solutions rather than merely an individual responsibility issue. |

## Concepts

Cross-cutting ideas, trends, and frameworks:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[capacity-hostile-environments]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Socio-technical contexts that restrict affordances for capacity development, encouraging shallow skilling and automation bias. |
| [[capacity-conducive-environments]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Contexts that afford and encourage opportunities for cultivating core human capacities through embodied, intersubjective habituation. |
| [[developmental-perfectionism]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Neo-Aristotelian approach to human flourishing where competent exercise of core capacities yields intrinsically valuable outcomes. |
| [[agential-control]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Ability to adjust action execution and initiate activities voluntarily, distinguishing skill from habit. |
| [[habituation]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Gradual process of skill inculcation through practice, attunement, intersubjectivity, and embodiment. |
| [[affordances-and-affordance-shrinkage]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Action possibilities formed by agent-environment relationships; shrinkage occurs when reduction becomes systematic and entrenched. |
| [[life-planning]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Activity of developing long-term goals and strategies, involving settling, coordinating, and self-deliberation functions. |

